<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea steps in to cap dollar rise - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea steps in to cap dollar rise - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea intervened in early morning interbank trading on Friday to support the won, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the central bank sold dollars after the won opened trading at the 845 level, compared with the base mid-rate of 842.70 set for the day based on Thursday's trading.</p>
</text>
